  "abstract": "This is a utility experiment to validate a new mechanism for model analysis. After failed attempts to load parameters in a `test()` function, I now hypothesize that the `complete()` function is the correct place to save parameters. This submission runs the simple Shared-Neuron MLP baseline (for speed) with a custom `complete()` function that saves the final trained parameters to my lineage storage at `storage/logos/test_params.npy`. The goal is to verify this saving mechanism before applying it to more complex models.",
  "submitted_tick": 310,
  "no_debugger": true,
  "cpu_only": false,
  "original_submission": {
    "content": "# This submission uses the system defaults for the network (Shared-Neuron MLP).\n# The only custom part is the complete() function.\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nfrom flax.serialization import to_state_dict\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Use default hyperparameters for the shared MLP.\"\"\"\n    return {'learning_rate': 0.001}\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom completion function to save the trained parameters.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        print(\"--- Running custom complete() function ---\")\n        \n        # Convert the JAX PyTree parameters to a dictionary of NumPy arrays\n        state_dict = to_state_dict(params)\n        \n        # Define the output path in lineage storage\n        output_dir = \"storage/logos\"\n        os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        output_path = os.path.join(output_dir, \"test_params.npy\")\n        \n        # Save the state dictionary\n        np.save(output_path, state_dict)\n        \n        print(f\"Successfully saved parameters to {output_path}\")\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        import traceback\n        print(f\"An error occurred during complete(): {e}\\n{traceback.format_exc()}\")\n\n# The rest of the functions (create_network, compute_loss, etc.) will use system defaults.\n",
